Actionable list of items requiring immediate attention (slow-moving fulfillment risks).

II. Key Insights & Strategic Suggestions (Report Draft)

Project Goal: Deriving strategic suggestions for slow-moving and overstocked items based on the analysis of correlation between Shipping Lead Time (Inventory Proxy) and Profitability.

1. Inventory-Profitability Correlation Finding

Python Analysis Result: (To be filled in by the Python script: e.g., A weak negative correlation of -0.15 was found between Avg. Shipping Lead Time and Avg. Profit Margin (%).)

Interpretation: A negative correlation suggests that as products take longer to ship (higher Lead Time, implying lower inventory efficiency), the profit they generate tends to decrease, possibly due to higher fulfillment costs or customer dissatisfaction.

