3. Strategic Recommendations for Slow-Moving/Overstocked Items

Triage High-Risk Stock: Immediately address products found in the High-Risk list (low margin, high shipping lead time). These items suffer from both low profitability and poor fulfillment efficiency. Focus on stocking them closer to high-demand regions.

Optimize Fulfillment: For categories with high shipping lead times but reasonable margins, investigate stocking levels and warehouse processes. The delay is not hitting profitability yet, but risks customer attrition.

Review Pricing Strategy: Products with adequate sales volume but very low margins may be priced too low relative to COGS. Review competitive pricing to ensure margins meet the minimum threshold.

Seasonal Pre-Stock: Use the seasonality analysis (Line Chart and Quarter Filter) to proactively stock high-demand items just before their peak season begins, reducing lead times during critical sales periods.
